Implement GL_POINT_SMOOTH in gl4es's GLES2 fixed-pipeline emulator.

gl4es tracked GL_POINT_SMOOTH but never acted on it. The enable round-tripped
through glPushAttrib/glPopAttrib (stack.c), answered glIsEnabled (enable.c),
and stored its hint (hint.c) -- but nothing consumed it, as the "todo: do
somthing with fpe?" comment above the enable.c proxy admits. Points therefore
rasterized as hard squares under WebGL regardless of the enable, since GLES2
has no point-antialiasing state of its own.

That breaks any scene drawing round sprites with large glPointSize: gl-repl's
glow-point examples (glow-sprites-blend-point-attenuation, lantern-festival,
jellyfish-gldepthmask-translucency, teapot-carousel, orrery-labels,
dusk-lighthouse-atoll) all enable GL_POINT_SMOOTH and render square blocks in
the Emscripten build while looking correct natively. gl-repl's own chrome hits
it too -- grid points, vertex overlays, guide handles and backdrop stars all
enable GL_POINT_SMOOTH from C.

Add a point_smooth bit to fpe_state_t so smooth and non-smooth points get
distinct cached programs, feed it from the enable.c proxy, and clamp it to 0
when not drawing points (mirroring the existing pointsprite clamping) so the
shader cache doesn't fragment on irrelevant state. In the generated fragment
shader, derive coverage from gl_PointCoord -- available for point primitives
independently of point-sprite enable -- discarding outside the unit radius and
folding a smoothstep edge into alpha.

The coverage multiply is emitted after the alpha test, matching desktop GL
where point antialiasing coverage applies at the blend stage rather than to
the value the alpha test sees. The edge feather is a fixed 0.85..1.0 of the
point radius: fwidth() would track the true pixel footprint but needs
OES_standard_derivatives, which the GLES2 profile can't assume.

Only the fixed-pipeline generator (fpe_FragmentShader) is patched;
fpe_CustomFragmentShader, used for ARB program conversion, is left alone.

Applied by scripts/web-deps.sh after cloning the pinned gl4es checkout.

